{"id": "sevt_01TaJJy3DQ4dqw1aZ1c8w3Cz", "content": [{"text": "**Finding: the 14:08 deploy `07000f4` introduced an N+1 query pattern in the checkout summary path, and it is still live.**\n\n**Deploys vs. metrics (checkout)**\n- **14:08:45** `07000f4` (alice, \"refactor order summary builder for readability\") deployed, status success. Checkout p99 starts climbing at 14:08 (77 \u2192 110 ms) and keeps rising, reaching ~420 ms by 14:29.\n- **14:26:00** `510eca7` (grace, \"rewrite order summary query path\") deployed, then rolled back at 14:29:10. Its diff only changes one log line in `middleware.py` to structured logging. It does not touch queries, so the rollback is not the fix.\n- **14:30** p99 steps from 423 ms to 3849 ms. This is about a minute after the rollback, so the deploy log does not explain the step.\n- `db_pool_utilization` climbs from ~0.13 at 14:00 to 1.0 at 14:39 and stays pinned there.\n- `error_rate` is near 0 until 14:39, then sits around 0.2\u20130.7%.\n\n**Diff of `07000f4`**\n- The old code ran one batched query: `SELECT * FROM order_items WHERE order_id IN (...)`, then grouped in memory.\n- The new code loops over the open orders and issues one `OrderItem` query per order. Each summary request now costs 1 + N database round trips.\n\n**Log confirmation**\n- The per-row query `order_items WHERE order_id = ?` first appears at 14:08:57, twelve seconds after the deploy. There are 4,090 occurrences in the log and 42 batch `IN (?)` queries.\n- Checkout request_end p99 rises in step with the per-row query volume.\n\n**Open questions**\n- The 14:30 step to ~3.8 s is not explained by either deploy. My best guess is that the pool hit its ceiling and requests began queuing, but I have not confirmed that from the logs.\n- `07000f4` is still deployed, so the regression is ongoing. Rolling back `07000f4` (or restoring the batched query) is the fix to verify. Rolling back only `510eca7` was not enough.\n\n**Root cause:** `07000f4` \u2014 the refactor replaced the batched `order_items` lookup with a per-order query, so each checkout summary issues N extra DB calls, saturating the checkout DB pool and pushing p99 from ~80 ms to multiple seconds.", "type": "text"}], "processed_at": "2026-10-14T12:01:54.787789Z", "type": "agent.message"}
